  "capacity_control": {
    "source": "use std::collections::HashMap;\nfn main() {\n    for count in [3,7,14,28] {\n        let mut map=HashMap::with_capacity(count);\n        for i in 0..count {map.insert(i,i);}\n        let before=map.capacity();\n        map.insert(0,999);\n        println!(\"size={count} before={before} after_insert={}\",map.capacity());\n        let mut map=HashMap::with_capacity(count);\n        for i in 0..count {map.insert(i,i);}\n        let before=map.capacity();\n        *map.get_mut(&0).unwrap()=999;\n        println!(\"size={count} before={before} after_replace={}\",map.capacity());\n    }\n}\n",
    "output": "size=3 before=3 after_insert=7\nsize=3 before=3 after_replace=3\nsize=7 before=7 after_insert=14\nsize=7 before=7 after_replace=7\nsize=14 before=14 after_insert=28\nsize=14 before=14 after_replace=14\nsize=28 before=28 after_insert=56\nsize=28 before=28 after_replace=28\n",
    "rustc": "rustc 1.96.0 (ac68faa20 2026-05-25)\nbinary: rustc\ncommit-hash: ac68faa20c58cbccd01ee7208bf3b6e93a7d7f96\ncommit-date: 2026-05-25\nhost: x86_64-apple-darwin\nrelease: 1.96.0\nLLVM version: 22.1.2\n"
  },
  "interpretation": "Identical baseline runs vary by one allocation/2464bytes in selected first-call cases. Toolchain HashMap.insert grows full tables even for existing keys; get_mut preserves capacity. Nested publication uses insert for replacements, making this consistent with order-dependent unnecessary growth. Candidate repeats and regression tests are still required for attribution/acceptance.",
  "audit_root": ".audit-evidence/nested-insertion-v2-2026-10-29",
